---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/apps/mailchimp';
const title = "Mailchimp for Shopify: audience sync, automation and SMS scope";
const desc = "Evaluate the connected audience, marketing permissions, billing exposure and queued messages before moving a Shopify program.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does Mailchimp currently connect to Shopify?",
    "answer": "Yes. Mailchimp documents a Shopify integration for customer and order data, ecommerce targeting and automation. Confirm the selected audience and current account features before connecting."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does an email plan make every Shopify customer eligible for SMS?",
    "answer": "No. SMS needs the applicable program approval, supported country and sender setup, plus the contact’s SMS subscription. Email and SMS permission are separate."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should a migration prove before launch?",
    "answer": "Reconcile audience identities and billing counts, resolve conflicting subscription states, and demonstrate that waiting promotions stop after purchase or opt-out while essential service messages continue."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/apps">App directory</a>
    <p class="badge mt-6">Operating review · November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p>
  </section>
  <article class="container prose-shopify pb-16">
    <h2>A current Shopify integration with more than newsletters</h2>
    <p><a class="link" href="https://mailchimp.com/help/connect-shopify/">Mailchimp for Shopify</a> connects store customer and order data for targeted ecommerce messaging and product recommendations. This can suit a team already using Mailchimp that wants store context in its marketing workflow. It should not be dismissed as an email-only accessory or prescribed beside a second email vendor by default.</p>
    <h2>Choose the audience before the initial sync</h2>
    <p>The <a class="link" href="https://mailchimp.com/help/mailchimp-shopify-syncing/">syncing guide</a> distinguishes initial and ongoing sync and carries subscription status into the selected audience. It also documents a consequential initial-sync case: an existing Mailchimp marketing opt-in can update the Shopify status to subscribed. Reconcile conflicting records before connection; compare source, timestamp and scope rather than assuming one export will preserve every status.</p>
    <h2>Proposed acceptance case: identity and audience boundaries</h2>
    <p>Create controlled records for a new subscriber, an existing opt-out, an order-only customer and the same address in a second audience. Snapshot their channel states before and after sync. Check which audience receives orders, whether identities duplicate and which status wins. Keep suppression evidence available during reconciliation. A successful customer-count match does not prove the selected people may receive a campaign.</p>
    <h2>Automation starts with event meaning</h2>
    <p>Shopify events supported in the syncing guide include product views, cart activity and checkout completion. These can support behavior-based marketing flows. Select the actual trigger and branching features available in your account, then inspect a browse-to-cart-to-purchase sequence. Repeated page views should not create uncontrolled parallel journeys. Set a purchase exit and verify its effect on already waiting messages rather than assuming a completed checkout empties every queue.</p>
    <h2>SMS eligibility is a separate decision</h2>
    <p><a class="link" href="https://mailchimp.com/help/about-sms-marketing/">SMS Marketing</a> has supported-country, registration and sender requirements. Do not infer universal country or plan access from an email subscription. The <a class="link" href="https://mailchimp.com/help/set-up-sms-marketing/">setup guide</a> ties the program to an audience and country-specific configuration. Confirm the actual account entitlement, approved sender and destinations before budgeting or collecting signups for a new market.</p>
    <h2>Keep marketing and service delivery distinct</h2>
    <p>Mailchimp documents <a class="link" href="https://mailchimp.com/help/about-transactional-email/">Marketing and Transactional</a> as different delivery paths. An automated message is not automatically transactional: inspect its purpose and content. Map order confirmations, account messages and promotional follow-ups to their real owner and entitlement. Preserve essential order service during a marketing migration; enabling an ecommerce integration does not demonstrate that a transactional API or service-message route is configured.</p>
    <h2>Proposed acceptance case: migrate the waiting queue</h2>
    <p>Inventory each old flow’s entry rule, wait, branch, offer expiry and purchase exit. Pause new entries, then inspect contacts already waiting. Use a controlled customer who buys during a cart delay and one who opts out before a scheduled promotion. Confirm both old and new systems prevent an inappropriate dispatch, while the required order confirmation still arrives once. Choose whether eligible waiting contacts drain or move; never enable both senders for the same job without a deliberate rule.</p>
    <h2>Reconcile audience costs before cleanup</h2>
    <p>Mailchimp’s <a class="link" href="https://mailchimp.com/help/create-audience/">audience documentation</a> explains that audiences do not share data and repeated contacts increase the total contact count. Its <a class="link" href="https://mailchimp.com/help/mailchimp-pricing-tiers/">pricing-tier guide</a> covers contact and send limits and additional charges. Review the actual agreement, billable contact states, archived records and peak-cycle counts. Do not erase suppression evidence merely to reduce a displayed audience total.</p>
    <h2>Model the migration month and the steady month</h2>
    <p>Request a quote for the reconciled audience and planned email volume, then add applicable SMS credits, sender/country costs, transactional delivery and the overlap period. Compare keeping the current setup with a proposed Mailchimp workflow using contribution per assigned eligible contact. Include merchandise, fulfillment and incremental labor/software costs; count discounts and returns once through net sales. Report separately how much savings comes from removing duplicate audiences versus changing message performance. No price or observed lift is asserted here.</p>
    <h2>A launch decision the operator can review</h2>
    <p>Keep a before/after audience ledger, accepted billing count and queue disposition for every flow. Release one intended journey first, watching event arrival, purchase exits and message duplication before expanding. Mailchimp may reduce operational fragmentation when its eligible tools cover the actual jobs; otherwise document the remaining sender boundary. Continue with <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing">pricing economics</a>, <a class="link" href="/guides/email-sms-coordination">channel ownership</a> and the <a class="link" href="/apps">app directory</a>.</p>
  </article>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
